; The ad-hoc table: a header vector of column keywords and a vector of rows,
; written as a bare two-element form with no head keyword at all. This is the
; shape for data with no compiled schema — a query result, a CSV import — and it
; is why ASN needs no `@table`, which would have cost two tokens for the `@`.
;
; canonical: ([:id :sku :price :currency] [[1 "SSD-1TB" 89.99 "USD"] [2 "RAM-32GB" 129.5 "USD"]])

([:id :sku :price :currency]
 [[1 "SSD-1TB"  89.99 "USD"]
  [2 "RAM-32GB" 129.5 "USD"]])
